Turbulence Modeling Resource — model definitions and benchmarks (@fd-tmr: 0, is #reference, #part-of @fd-sources) { r_42VW512D9MG3Z0SBJ78N7DAPE6
Turbulence Model Benchmarking Working Group, with NASA contributors. [Current resource](https://tmbwg.github.io/turbmodels/) · [NASA's relocation notice](https://www.nasa.gov/nasa-turbulence-modeling-resource/) · [NASA-hosted large files](https://www.nasa.gov/reference/turbulence-modeling-resource-large-files/).

Read complete definitions of the selected model and named variant, its verification cases, grid studies and applicable validation data. Reproduce a benchmark before using the model for a new claim. Distinguish model implementation verification, numerical uncertainty and comparison with experiments.

The site moved from the NASA Langley address to the working group's GitHub site on 24 February 2026. Model variants, constants and conventions are part of the citation. Large-file download restrictions may require the linked NASA mirror. Public data are supplied with source-specific provenance and limitations, not a guarantee of universal accuracy or one blanket licence. No benchmark files are bundled.

**Return:** [Fluid dynamics sources — books, courses, methods and physical evidence](../Sources.lingua#r_3Y3TVV9VQAB50M2ZSECK5JTYVG).
} r_42VW512D9MG3Z0SBJ78N7DAPE6
